worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:103:**Launcher `depth_canon_launch.sh`** — adapted from the reviewed exp_17 launcher with its r3 blocking findings applied AND the review-H9 gates: (1) reviewed-tree binding: pin **HEAD** and content-pin every file on the training path (`train.py`, `defaults.ini`, `src/data/*.py`, `src/models/*.py`, `src/training/*.py`, `src/inference/*.py`, `AR_md.py`, dataset config, split, VAE, control + arm config, the DINOv3 gate script) via a committed manifest; (2) smoke evidence must carry the same HEAD + manifest hash + `config contract OK`, and **a smoke is re-run after any review-driven source change**; (3) no `pipefail` around `tr | grep` — the log is read once into a variable after `wait`-draining the `tee` FIFO; (4) NaN/Inf check in FULL mode too; (5) **run-owned checkpoints**: FULL refuses a non-empty run namespace, every accepted checkpoint must be newer than the launch epoch, the cadence set must be exactly {2500, …, 40000}, foreign/stale files abort; (6) **NAS gate on the save filesystem**: mount identity (`findmnt`/`df` of the save path shows the CIFS share), a write-probe file, free space ≥ 30 GiB; (7) pinned smoke-projection threshold ≤ 60 h (**v14:** ≤ 120 h, because a shared card roughly halves the uncontended 0.259 opt-steps/s — the bound is a sanity cap on a co-tenant launch, not a speed target); **v10 (Codex r3b):** (8) GPU gate = ≥ 22.5 GiB free on BOTH cards **and zero foreign compute processes** on GPUs 0/1 (`nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps`; HIGH 7) — the launcher kills nothing; **v11:** every nvidia-smi query is strict (exit status checked apart from stdout, exactly one numeric memory row per card, malformed or unknown-uuid rows refuse) and every GPU-gate refusal exits with the DEDICATED **rc 7** (the watcher's only transient signal); **v12 (Codex rA2 HIGH 1/2):** rc 7 is emitted by ONE function (`gpu_refuse`) and an EXIT trap remaps any other exit 7 — `train.py`'s own status included — to the terminal **rc 8**, so a trainer failure is never retried; after the gate the co-tenancy disclosure issues NO further nvidia-smi query (it prints the strict gate's validated answers: free MiB + uuid per card, compute processes on other cards). **v14 (SHARED-GPU launch mode, ordered by Yixun 2026-10-25 ≈ 22:40 EDT — verbatim "please launch exp_25 if we have enough GPU free usage", then the AskUserQuestion choice "Relax the gates and launch shared now"):** the gate is MEMORY-ONLY: pinned `MIN_GPU_FREE_MIB=12288` (12 GiB per card; measured need of the identical `--batch-size 32 --num-gpus 2` recipe on this box: 5.9–6.6 GiB per rank in exp_14's smoke, ≈ 10.3 GiB per card for the exp_13 vanilla-B arm; the old 22.5 GiB floor was a margin, never a measurement), pinned `GPU_OCCUPANCY_POLICY=shared` (the other value, `idle`, restores the v10 refusal), the strict nvidia-smi parsing of v11 kept in full; foreign compute processes on GPU 0/1 are DISCLOSED (pid, card, used MiB, cwd) in the launch log and in the SMOKE evidence (`gpu_policy`, `min_gpu_free_mib`, `free_mib_at_launch`, `co_tenants_at_launch`) instead of refused; rc 7 stays reserved for the memory floor and unclean queries. Consequences carried as result disclosures: the FULL run and the campaign execute next to Yixun's xRIR exp_13/exp_28 chains (32 GiB each, 100 % utilization) and user dzheng's lanes — speed only, never the numbers; OOM risk in both directions (a co-tenant growing past the free memory kills whichever process allocates last; this launcher still never signals anything); the watcher's poll predicate mirrors the policy (foreign processes logged, memory floor decides). The eval campaign runs its lanes with `ALLOW_SHARED_GPU=1` (A6 opt-in, exercised by this instruction). Launcher exit codes: 0 ok · 2 a gate refused · 3 banner missing · 4 non-finite / SMOKE verdict FAILED · 5 checkpoint set wrong · 6 endpoint or two-rank start missing · 7 GPU gate (transient) · 8 a remapped 7 · anything else = `train.py`'s own status; (9) the interpreter is **enforced** (`command -v python` must resolve under `envs/flac/bin`; HIGH 6); (10) **tie-audit gate (BLOCKING 1; v11 = Codex rA A1 + rB B1):** SMOKE and FULL both refuse unless the committed, PINNED rung-3 audit report `depth_canon_tie_audit.json` + `.sha256` (in the pin set, committed at HEAD) passes THE one predicate `depth_canon_audit_gate.py` (`validate_tie_audit(audit_path, repo_root) -> (ok, problems, summary)`; CLI 0/1/2): sidecar, type-strict schema, `verdict PASS`, zero survivors/errors, full non-`--limit` coverage of the three splits, registered item counts, `dirty_code == ""`, no harness tag in production, the expected 9,650 unique map paths derived from the split JSONs through the audit script's own enumeration (path-set equality, no duplicates, typed rows), per-split census consistent with the rows, content hashes of the audit script / operator / `dataset.py` / `AR_md.py` / dataset configs / split JSONs, and a **re-hash of every current depth map** against the row hashes (8 threads inside a KILLABLE child process — the gate itself in `--rehash-worker` mode, own session — under the registered **900 s** wall-clock deadline `REHASH_DEADLINE_S`, no CLI or env override; read-only NAS, ≈ 2 min 15 s per launch; a timeout SIGKILLs the child's process group and fails closed, as do a nonzero child, no JSON or a malformed answer → launcher rc 2 → watcher FAILED; v12, Codex rA2 NIT 4). The gate module's sha256 joins the SMOKE→FULL content bind. Harness mode accepts a harness-tagged synthetic report only under `DEPTH_CANON_HARNESS` against a harness-provided contract file; (11) **SMOKE evidence (BLOCKING 2):** mandatory parsed finite loss and the wrapper's rank-0 fit-end line `canonicalize latency rank0 batches=<int> samples=<int> total_s=<float> mean_ms_per_batch=<float>` (no `null` fields); (12) the SMOKE→FULL bind is **content-scoped** (NIT): FULL requires the smoke's pin-manifest sha256 and training-closure content to equal the current tree's, so record-only commits between SMOKE and FULL are safe, while `EXPECT_HEAD` stays HEAD-identity for the launch itself (hence the freeze rule in §11 A5). Pin closure adds `FLAC_AR_BV.json` / `FLAC_AR_BF.json` (opened by the DINOv3 gate; HIGH 5) and, in v11, the committed tie-audit report + sidecar → **48 entries**; `assert_arm_configs.py::assert_vit_pin` now hash-pins the whole DINOv3 snapshot file set incl. `config.json` (Codex rA H5). W&B writes a repo-local `wandb/` directory (gitignored) — documented, not a gate. MODE=SMOKE (25 steps, cadence 10⁶ ⇒ no checkpoint, own namespace) → MODE=FULL requires a passing SMOKE on record. Guard suite `depth_canon_guardtests.sh` drives the launcher's real branches with `DRY_RUN=1` and synthetic logs in `mktemp -d` — never the production evidence directory.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:105:**Auto-launch watcher `depth_canon_autolaunch.sh` (v10, round 3d; A5).** Armed by the Planner once every gate is closed; it waits for a valid GO token (`depth_canon_GO.token`: `head` == `git rev-parse HEAD`, `manifest_sha256` == sha256 of `depth_canon_pins.sha256`; re-checked before every launch) and for 3 consecutive clean 60-s polls (zero compute processes on GPUs 0 and 1 and ≥ 23,040 MiB free on each; an `nvidia-smi` failure counts as dirty), then runs `MODE=SMOKE EXPECT_HEAD=<head>` and, on rc 0, `MODE=FULL` with the same head. A SMOKE that fails on the launcher's GPU / foreign-process gate is retried (≤ 5×, counter reset); any other failure is terminal (`FAILED`, FULL never attempted). Phases (WAITING_TOKEN → WAITING_GPU → SMOKE_RUNNING → FULL_RUNNING → DONE | FAILED) are written atomically to `depth_canon_autolaunch_state.json`; log `depth_canon_<TS>_autolaunch.log`; single instance (flock); flac interpreter enforced; it contains no `kill`, writes nothing outside the experiment folder and never touches the NAS itself. It is outside the training closure and therefore NOT in the pin manifest. It invokes the launcher with literal `MB=32 ACC=1 DRY_RUN=0` and scrubs every harness-only variable (v11, Codex rA W5b); the interpreter check is the launcher's exact pinned path; the token is exactly four newline-terminated `key=value` lines and nothing else (every logical line counts, blank ones too: keys = lines = newlines = 4; v12, Codex rA2 NIT 5) with a full ISO-8601 `issued` (what `date -Iseconds` prints) and `token_ok` also requires the pinned paths, the pins file, the launcher, the pin generator and the audit gate to be clean (a dirty file → WAITING_TOKEN, never terminal); transient = the launcher's rc 7 only (no text matching); the outer tee is drained at exit. Detached with `setsid nohup`; the Planner arms a Monitor on the state file.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:133:**v10 (round 3c as built).** Cells are data: `depth_canon_cells.json` (230 rows = T 10, T-dup 2, C4+45 8, R 10, D-i 2, D-ii 2, S 10, P1-pin 28, YAW-pin 38, TRAJ 120; generated by `depth_canon_make_cells.py`, names injective through `build_output_paths`; `--blocks` selects the required set so A1 is a switch, `--no-dump-blocks` implements A3; flags written out explicitly incl. `--batch-size 64 --device cuda` and `--rotate-mode fixed --rotate-deg θ` on every fixed cell; YAW-pin uses `exp_15_yaw_aug_claude/FLAC_AR_YAWAUG.json`, byte-equal to the YAW checkpoint's embedded config). `depth_canon_eval_run.sh`: gates (lock, flac interpreter, **strict HEAD pin** `EXPECT_HEAD` = the campaign's one evaluator pin — kept strict by Planner decision: no commits on the branch during the ≈ 23 h campaign, records go to the FLAC checkout; committed-tree check; config pins; dump ROOT on the NAS share), checkpoints sha256-verified once per path against the NAS manifest and linked into a local farm `outputs_FLAC/exp25_depth_canon/<ARM>/` so metrics never land in `ar_40k_endpoints/`; two GPU lanes; the complete-and-verified resume predicate (marker + `depth_canon_collect.verify_cell`, which reads each dump once), quarantine of anything else, a required per-cell receipt `<stem>.cell.json` (checkpoint sha checked before the run, configs, argv, pin, lane, rc), TRAJ last. **Eval GPU policy (A6, landed in rB-F1):** a lane is used only when its card has ≥ 10 GiB free AND no foreign compute process (uuid-mapped, fail-closed queries, re-checked right before each spawn); `ALLOW_SHARED_GPU=1` (explicit opt-in by Yixun) relaxes the occupancy part only — **exercised for the whole exp_25 campaign by Yixun's 2026-10-25 shared-launch instruction (v14).** **v11 driver integrity (Codex rB B3/B4):** the relevant-tree content digest is taken at start, before every spawn and after every cell — any change is PIN DRIFT, exit 4, no further spawns, running cells finish; checkpoints are copied into a content-addressed verified cache `<farm>/.ckpt_cache/<sha>.ckpt` (hash while copying, 0444, atomic rename, free-space gate ≈ 14 GB) and hard-linked into the farm (an existing cache entry must satisfy the immutable contract — regular file, mode 0444, the source's size — and is fully re-hashed at staging AND immediately before EACH spawn; the post-run MEASURED sha256 goes into the receipt; r3c-style symlink farms are refused). **v12 (Codex rB2 B4):** `eval_FLAC.py` reads the checkpoint ONCE into memory, hashes that buffer and deserializes that same buffer (`torch.load(io.BytesIO(buf), map_location='cpu')`, arguments otherwise unchanged), recording `ckpt_sha256_loaded` + `ckpt_bytes_loaded` in every metrics record right after the base keys (records built without it stay byte-identical); `build_receipt` refuses unless loaded == measured == manifest sha and the loaded length == the driver's post-run `stat` (`--ckpt-bytes`); `verify_cell` requires record == receipt for both fields; `--nas-retention-audit` refuses `--dump-check receipt` (rB2 NIT). **Receipt `<stem>.cell.json` (A7, landed):** written only after the post-run full verification; carries the campaign/spawn/post digests, the checkpoint shas (expected + measured + loaded, with the loaded length), `artifact_sha256` of the metrics / `.stream.json` / `.canon.json`, and `dump_evidence` (verified dump manifest sha256, n, shape, dtype, waveform sha256, marker); `verify_cell(dump_check='receipt')` and `gen_model_comparison.py` validate OFFLINE from the committed files; `depth_canon_collect.py --nas-retention-audit` checks the bulk dumps separately. `depth_canon_collect.py`: `verify_cell` (protocol + B2 binding fields per cell class, manifest-level dump check), pairs by (arm, K, seed, step) with the `input_hash` proof, Tier 1 per-position hash equality + recomputed `canonical_depth_hash`, Tier 2 from the dumps via `depth_canon_stats`, Tier 3 (`Δ_C4`, 45° probe, seed-paired `Δ_R` on input_hash-equal pairs only), the table block (mean ± sd, item-weighted and per-scene), TRAJ grid, tie counts per cell and per split, `--partial` labels every heading PARTIAL and lists the missing cells; writes `depth_canon_results.{md,json}`. **Tier-2 control mapping (registered):** 45° → d64, 90° → d128, 180° → d256, 270° → d384, random → random; the pooled control p99 is the reference; matched-offset AND pooled rules plus the 1e-2 cap are all applied (fail-closed reading of "control p99"). The collector accepts as the Tier-2 reference **only** a probe artifact marked `registered: true` (run without `--diagnostic`, sidecar-verified, bound to the CANON@40k checkpoint sha); diagnostic probes are refused (Codex r3b HIGH 4; probe exit codes 0 registered PASS / 1 verdict FAIL / 2 refused / 6 diagnostic); **v11 (Codex rB B5):** a dirty tree is a registered deviation; the collector's `PROBE_CONTRACT` checks the evaluator pin == campaign pin, exact registered arguments, config + split hashes, load protocol, stream census, and renders `eps_cond = v; registered threshold 1e-05: PASS/FAIL` (missing / non-finite ε → artifact invalid). **Pairing (v11, Codex rB NIT):** `context_ids` has exactly K entries per item; strict uniqueness is NOT required because `AR_md` draws with replacement when a room has fewer than K other sources (520 of 6,337 unseen K = 8 targets; identical across the 11 exp_15 streams checked) — the registered rule is that every cell of one (split, K) repeats on the same targets; identical generative noise follows from the execution protocol (same arm/K/step/seed, batch size, census under the pinned evaluator), not from the hash preimage. The shared-map overlap count is derived from the validated audit and compared with the registered 1,093 items / 112 maps. `gen_model_comparison.py` gains the `exp25` contract (rows CANON / P1-pin / YAW-pin at the exp_25 pin, YAW-pin labelled re-measured; validation through `verify_cell`; a round = two-K pair at one pin); additive only.
