- **C7 — RESOLVED as implementation, with a mandatory pre-token action.** DRY_RUN skips: NAS write probe (line 343), live GPU gate (372), W&B identity (445), and launch/post-run/evidence generation (483). Independent coverage: non-DRY harness cases exercise successful/failed write probes, GPU branches, evidence writing, and post-run checks; the W&B path has only the reported standalone identity check, not a committed log. I did not repeat it because this was static review. It must be rerun immediately before every actual token as required by [plan_depth_canon.md:187](/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-25-depth-canon/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:187).

- **C8 — RESOLVED with registered limitations.** The 25-step projection measures the currently contended rate, but only over approximately steps 10–25; it is a point-in-time sanity check, not a 40k forecast under bursty neighbors. Co-tenant processes cannot automatically inject into this launcher’s tee, namespace, or evidence; deliberate same-path writes remain outside the admission threat model. `COT_N[AIDX]` is safe, empty-array expansion is safe under Bash 5.2.21, and the quoted four-argument protocol preserves cwd spaces and `?`.

